            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="1000" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11 Am 8/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-13T16:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 14—10:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Department’s 22, November 30, 6 p.m. President’s answer received today states
                    that by reason of autonomy of municipality he will not be able to intervene but
                    that he has written the municipality <pb facs="1001" n="877" xml:id="pg877"/>
                    transcribing at the same time the desires of Amsinck and Company and suggesting
                    to the president of the municipality the necessity that the municipality comply
                    with the arrangement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
